From 32dd60282ec18a0d1f731ebfb300027e0a40d996 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:38:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] elf: Terminate the .eh_frame section of ld.so

ld.so is linked from librtld.os alone, so unlike libc.so and every
other shared object glibc builds it never gets sofini.os, and its
.eh_frame ends in the last FDE's CFI opcodes with no zero
terminator.  On MicroBlaze the section ends "05 9c 04 9d 03 9f 01 00".

That goes unnoticed wherever ld.so has an .eh_frame_hdr search
table, because the unwinder then never walks the section linearly.
MicroBlaze cannot have one: GCC uses DW_EH_PE_aligned pointers in PIC
code there, and ld refuses to build the table for that encoding
("FDE encoding ... prevents .eh_frame_hdr table being created").
libgcc falls back to linear_search_fdes, which stops only at a
zero-length entry, so any unwind that reaches a frame in ld.so walks
past the end of .eh_frame into whatever is mapped next until it
trips on garbage and aborts in read_encoded_value_with_base.

The frame it reaches is __libc_start_main's return address, which
_dl_start_user sets to _dl_fini - 8, so every _Unwind_Backtrace or
forced unwind that goes through main aborts on MicroBlaze
(elf/tst-unwind-main).

Link a terminator into ld.so.  sofini.os as built for libc cannot be
used directly: with symbol-hacks.h it carries undefined references
to __GI_memcpy and friends that ld.so does not define, and the -z
defs sanity check rejects it.  Build an rtld flavour, rtld-sofini.os,
from the same source and link it last.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 elf/Makefile | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/elf/Makefile b/elf/Makefile
index 4d1032bb2a..8b10d7f591 100644
--- a/elf/Makefile
+++ b/elf/Makefile
@@ -1677,7 +1677,14 @@ generated += librtld.map librtld.mk rtld-libc.a librtld.os.map
 
 z-now-yes = -Wl,-z,now
 
-$(objpfx)ld.so: $(objpfx)librtld.os $(ld-map)
+# The .eh_frame terminator.  sofini.os as built for libc carries the
+# symbol-hacks redirections to __GI_* symbols that ld.so cannot resolve,
+# so build an rtld flavour of it.  It must come last in the link.
+libof-rtld-sofini := rtld
+$(objpfx)rtld-sofini.os: sofini.c $(before-compile)
+	$(compile-command.c)
+
+$(objpfx)ld.so: $(objpfx)librtld.os $(objpfx)rtld-sofini.os $(ld-map)
 # Link into a temporary file so that we don't touch $@ at all
 # if the sanity check below fails.
 	$(LINK.o) -nostdlib -nostartfiles -shared -o $@.new		\
